	abstract = {DeepSeek is presented as an artificial intelligence tool that can assist with challenging coding tasks or data analysis, while ChatGPT is emphasized for its potential as a generative AI model focused primarily for customer support, educational tasks, etc. This chapter investigates the disruptive nature of AI models, namely DeepSeek and ChatGPT, on the software engineering discipline. It begins with descriptions and comparisons of each model's architectures and functionality, specifically mentioning DeepSeek's Mixture-of-Experts (MoE), which assists with efficiency in performing technical tasks, and ChatGPT's Generative Pre-trained Transformer (GPT) architecture, which excels in producing conversational feedback. Additionally, the chapter elaborates on the significant features of both models, including but not limited to code generation, debugging, and technical documentation. Moreover, it explores the variety of ways software engineers can use AI models, including how these incorporated AI models can help streamline work processes and contribute to software engineers’ productivity. A discussion about the ethical considerations around the use and integration of these AI models into the field of software engineering is outlined, focusing on responsible use and bias. Further, as these mentioned artificial intelligence technologies will evolve, a future trends discussion is identified with the potential of how these models can redefine the approaches associated with the computing discipline. As software engineers combine the models’ capabilities, software engineers can produce better classroom applications responding to society's increased reliance on technology. © 2026},
