	affiliations = {National School of Applied Sciences, Sultan Moulay Slimane University, Lipim Laboratory, Khouribga, Morocco; Higher School of Arts and Crafts, Sultan Moulay Slimane University, Lasti Laboratory, Khouribga, Morocco; Hassan Ii University, Aimce Laboratory, Casablanca, Morocco},
	abstract = {The emergence of Large Language Models (LLMs) has revolutionized software engineering due to their ability to understand and generate natural language. Current approaches to test case automation using LLMs, relying solely on focal methods or text, struggle to capture expected behaviors, edge cases, and errors, and are poorly suited for Test-Driven Development (TDD). In this context, we propose an approach that combines text and focal methods for test case generation, using comments within the code alongside the logic of the target method. By leveraging the LLaMA 3-8B model, prompt engineering techniques, and evaluation with an LLM acting as a judge, our method aims to automate and improve test case generation. Tested on open-source projects, it successfully generated 7,606 test cases, achieving a 97% syntax correction rate. © 2025 IEEE.},
