	abstract = {Generative artificial intelligence (AI) has quickly changed the current trend of the software development process. In particular, AI-assisted pair programming has emerged as a revolutionary concept that partners with human creativity to enhance collaboration, boost productivity, and improve code quality. Introducing AI into a tra ditional team practice like pair programming leads to substantive gains because the coder works alongside the AI programming partner. Generative AI tools actively tribute to the software development process by providing real-time suggestions, erating code snippets, identifying errors, and offering explanations based on the latest advancements and best practices. These AI systems must adapt to the coding ment, thereby offering valuable support in problem-solving while bridging knowledge gaps and assisting in decision-making processes. This chapter explores various aspects of generative AI-assisted pair programming and its potential to reshape the way velopers work, learn, and create. The chapter describes the elements of generative AI- assisted pair programming, its architecture, and its introduction into contemporary platforms for development. Various stages of code development and the impact of AI in these stages are discussed. This chapter explores both the benefits and limitations of AI-assisted pair programming, along with strategies to overcome those limitations. This chapter also examines the impact of this technology on team productivity, edge sharing, and the training of developers. © 2025 Walter de Gruyter GmbH, Berlin/Boston, Genthiner Straße 13, 10785 Berlin.},
	author_keywords = {AI in software engineering; AI-assisted pair programming; code generation; collaborative software devel opment; Generative AI},
