	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105022017408?origin=resultslist},
	affiliations = {Mary Matha Arts and Science College, Mananthavady, PGand Research Department of Computer Science, India},
	abstract = {The advancement of Large Language Models (LLMs) has an important role in software development. This study provides a comparative analysis of state-of-the-art code generation models, including CodeGeex, CodeLlama, StarCoder, PanGu-Coder, WizardCoder, CodeT5+, DeepSeek-Coder, and CodeGen-Mono, looking on their architectural frameworks, evaluation metrics, pros and cons. The study examines the most widely used evaluation metrics such as HumanEval and MBPP, based on Pass@1 and Pass@100 scores. The findings shows that PanGu-Coder, WizardCoder, and DeepSeek-Coder have high accuracy in general-purpose code generation, models like CodeLlama and CodeGen Mono excel in Python-Based problem-solving tasks. These models also face challenges such as high computational costs, limited real-world adaptability, and the need for fine-tuning for industry-specific applications. The study also highlights the research gaps, with the need for more efficient models with less resource requirements, improved multilanguage support and better integration into real-world software development workflows. This study aims to contribute to the ongoing development of much better code generation tool development in case of development cost, multi-language support etc. © 2025 IEEE.},
