	affiliations = {Wuhan Textile University, School of Computer Science and Artificial Intelligence, Wuhan, China; Wuhan Textile University, Engineering Research Center of Hubei Province for Clothing Information, Wuhan, China},
	abstract = {With the increasing complexity of software tools, enhancing development efficiency and automation levels is of paramount importance. However, current automation tools typically focus on one or a few specific stages in software development, and there are still deficiencies in functionality coverage, intelligent support, and interpretability. To bridge this gap, this article presents LLMSDH, an integrated software-assisted development tool based on large language models (LLMs). LLMSDH is designed to encompass various key phases of the software development lifecycle, thereby driving automation and efficiency in the development process. The tool provides a web-based user interface at http://123.207.10.218:8501, which streamlines requirements analysis, modeling, and comprehensive development management, encompassing everything from code generation to defect detection. Additionally, LLMSDH automatically generates technical reports to analyze and profile projects, assisting developers in refining project presentations and promotions. Significantly, LLMSDH prioritizes the interpretability of its outputs, thereby enhancing user trust and satisfaction. The source code for this tool is publicly accessible on GitHub at https://github.com/NICERTYU/LLMSDH.git. And an instructional video is also available on Bilibili at https://space.bilibili.com/1155790507?spm_id_from=333.788.0.0. © 2025 IEEE.},
