	abstract = {This study examines the shortcomings and restrictions of web-based platforms for developing applications, including website builders, no-code app builders, and e-commerce platforms, in terms of their ability to satisfy the distinct needs and rationale of various business types. Even if these platforms are practical and simple to use, they frequently fall short in offering tailored software solutions that meet the unique requirements of companies. The research emphasizes how difficult it is for startups and small companies to find qualified engineers and how expensive it is to keep up internal development teams. The dangers and restrictions of using website builders and comparable platforms are also covered, including the possibility of vendor lock-in, problems with data control, and a lack of flexibility when it comes to adding special features or procedures. The goal of this research is to offer useful insights for companies who want to use web-based applications in their operations by identifying and analyzing these limits. In the end, it aims to further knowledge of the constraints of current development platforms and assist companies in making decisions that will maximize their online presence and operations. © 2024 IEEE.},
