	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105002337838?origin=resultslist},
	affiliations = {Tianjin University of Technology and Education, School of Information Technology Engineering, Tianjin, China},
	abstract = {With the growing demand for efficient code generation and maintenance in software development, model-driven development and SQLcontrol development have gradually become important choices in modern enterprise applications. This paper focuses on JDL (Jhipster Domain Language) in JHipster and MyBatis-Plus, comparing their core technical features in data model generation, database interaction, development efficiency, and applicable scenarios to analyze the advantages and disadvantages of these two development models. Through experiments, this paper evaluates the performance of JDL and MyBatis-Plus in terms of development efficiency, code maintainability, and system performance, while further exploring how to leverage the strengths of both frameworks in mixed development scenarios to address complex project requirements. Experimental results show that JDL is better suited for rapid development and highly automated, standardized scenarios, while MyBatis-Plus excels in handling high complexity and fine-grained control requirements. This paper summarizes the applicable scenarios of these two development models and their combined usage, providing developers with detailed technical guidance for technology selection and offering recommendations for optimizing future database development tools.  © 2024 IEEE.},
