	abstract = {The software development method of VSC-HVDC valve control device based on traditional handwritten code has disadvantages of low product reliability, long debugging cycle and being unfavorable for subsequent product maintenance. In order to solve these problems, a visual programming method with model design as the core is used to develop the valve control device of VSC-HVDC. The development process based on model design method, the valve control sequence control model and the overall control strategy model of circulating current suppression are described in detail. Then, the model is simulated and verified, and code generation and deployment are carried out. Finally, the actual operation test is carried out in combination withKunbei-Liubei-Longmen DC transmission project, and the engineering application of the software results is completed. The software development method based on model design integrates control strategy verification and code generation, which not only improves development efficiency and product reliability but also has strong operability and high maintainability. © 2021 Editorial Department of Zhejiang Electric Power. All rights reserved.},
